WEBVTT

NOTE English translation of the Vietnamese narration script. Timing is distributed proportionally within each slide segment, since the narration itself is in Vietnamese.

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.522
Hello everyone, this is the quick revision video for Chapter One:

2
00:00:04.522 --> 00:00:06.639
An overview of business communication.

3
00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:11.031
Over about four minutes, we'll go through everything covered in class together,

4
00:00:11.031 --> 00:00:14.200
so you can check for yourself how well you've grasped it.

5
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:17.839
First, the concept.

6
00:00:17.839 --> 00:00:21.452
Communication is the process of exchanging information,

7
00:00:21.452 --> 00:00:26.380
ideas and feelings between people in order to achieve a particular purpose.

8
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:30.928
Business communication is communication tied to the business process:

9
00:00:30.928 --> 00:00:35.477
between a company and its customers, its partners, regulatory bodies,

10
00:00:35.477 --> 00:00:38.245
and among members within the organisation.

11
00:00:38.245 --> 00:00:44.700
Remember this: every business communication is aimed at a specific work objective, not casual chat.

12
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.903
Business communication has four characteristics.

13
00:00:49.903 --> 00:00:51.947
One, it always has a clear purpose.

14
00:00:51.947 --> 00:00:54.490
Two, it involves diverse parties and roles:

15
00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:58.807
at the same time we communicate with customers, superiors and colleagues,

16
00:00:58.807 --> 00:01:01.350
each requiring its own standard of conduct.

17
00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:04.530
Three, it is bound by interests and legal obligations:

18
00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:08.358
words and documents can create duties, contracts and liabilities.

19
00:01:08.358 --> 00:01:12.656
And four, it is both a science and an art: there are principles to learn,

20
00:01:12.656 --> 00:01:15.600
but they must be applied flexibly to be effective.

21
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.898
This is the most important diagram in the chapter.

22
00:01:20.898 --> 00:01:25.523
The communication process passes through five stages: the sender forms an idea,

23
00:01:25.523 --> 00:01:29.796
encodes it into speech or writing, the message travels through a channel,

24
00:01:29.796 --> 00:01:32.664
the receiver decodes it, and then gives feedback.

25
00:01:32.664 --> 00:01:36.636
Noise can intrude at any stage: background noise, a poor connection,

26
00:01:36.636 --> 00:01:40.373
language and cultural differences, prejudice, negative emotions.

27
00:01:40.373 --> 00:01:41.898
When a conversation fails,

28
00:01:41.898 --> 00:01:45.300
trace back through each stage to find where it broke down.

29
00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:51.944
As for the means of communication, besides spoken and written language,

30
00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:56.965
we also communicate non-verbally: eye contact, facial expressions, smiles, gestures,

31
00:01:56.965 --> 00:02:00.671
posture, distance, dress, tone of voice, and even punctuality.

32
00:02:00.671 --> 00:02:04.501
Mehrabian's research shows that for emotionally-loaded messages,

33
00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:09.229
words account for only about seven percent, tone of voice thirty-eight percent,

34
00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:12.102
and body language as much as fifty-five percent.

35
00:02:12.102 --> 00:02:15.300
So don't let your body say the opposite of your words.

36
00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:21.921
Finally, the five communication principles you need to know by heart.

37
00:02:21.921 --> 00:02:22.411
Respect.

38
00:02:22.411 --> 00:02:23.940
Goodwill and cooperation.

39
00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:27.061
Listen and understand before stating your own view.

40
00:02:27.061 --> 00:02:32.200
Fit the context: the right role, the right time, the right place, the right channel.

41
00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:37.400
And uphold standards and keep your word — trustworthiness is itself a business asset.

42
00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.961
To sum up, three things to remember.

43
00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:45.863
First, business communication has a purpose and rules of its own.

44
00:02:45.863 --> 00:02:50.484
Second, effectiveness is decided by all five stages and by controlling noise.

45
00:02:50.484 --> 00:02:54.266
Third, non-verbal communication is more powerful than we think.

46
00:02:54.266 --> 00:02:59.368
Go ahead and do the forty multiple-choice questions for Chapter One to test yourself.

47
00:02:59.368 --> 00:03:01.889
See you in the Chapter Two revision video.
